cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this brief, its taxonomy or the explorer, please cite it as below."
title: "The Value of Open Research Information: Ten Transformative Benefits (Barcelona Declaration WG7-TF2)"
abstract: >-
  What research systems gain when information about research is open, as a brief
  and an interactive explorer: ten benefit dimensions in three axes (Quality &
  Trust, Collaboration & Innovation, Impact & Relevance) that lead to trustworthy
  research, sustainable innovation and societal impact. Contribution to Task Force
  2 of Working Group 7 of the Barcelona Declaration on Open Research Information.
  The brief is at version 0.4, a working document. Two benefits (B9 Strategic
  Steering & Institutional Autonomy and B10 Reuse & Collective Action) and the
  changes to B1, B2, B4, B7 and B8 are proposals put to WG7-TF2, not decisions the task
  force has taken. The explorer runs entirely in the browser and is available in English,
  German and Spanish.
  It runs at https://rijdho.github.io/barcelona-wg7-tf2/.
